    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_7",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Wernher Magnus Maximilian Freiherr von Braun (March 23, 1912 – June 16, 1977) was a German, later American, aerospace engineer and space architect credited with inventing the V-2 rocket for Nazi Germany and the Saturn V for the United States. He was the leading figure in the development of rocket technology in Germany and the father of rocket technology and space science in the United States.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
      "value": 0.9999999963537184,
      "temperature": 0.9999999963537184,
